    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15053" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀριμασποί</span></b> , οἱ,
		Scythian word, meaning <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one-eyed,</i> derived by <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.27
			</span></i> from <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄριμα</span></b> 
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕν, σποῦ</span>
			
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφθαλμός</span>
			; by Eust.ad <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				31
			</span></i> from <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρί</span></b> 
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕν, μασπός</span>
			
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφθαλμός</span>
			 : 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀ. ἱπποβάμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					805
				</span></i>
			.</div>
